- op: discuss  # 53a9
  at: '2026-03-18T08:34:04Z'  # 53a9
  by: agent  # 53a9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 53a9
  clock: 11  # 53a9
  nonce: 53a9  # 53a9
  message: "Investigation update: GraphQL codegen (gqlgen for Go, git-bug): The Go analyzer's 'implements' edges already connect resolver implementations to generated interfaces (154 implements edges in git-bug). The graph IS traversable from schema to implementation. No additional linker work needed for Go gqlgen.\n\nRemaining uninvestigated: (1) TypeScript graphql-codegen SDK hooks, (2) gRPC codegen Python/TS, (3) wasm_bindgen facades. Apollo-server's codegen.yml generates TypeScript type declarations (not SDK functions), so the codegen gap there is minimal — the actual GraphQL operations use template literals that the existing linker already detects.\n\nUpdated assessment: codegen wrapper tracing is partially addressed. Go gqlgen works. TypeScript/Python codegen wrappers remain a theoretical gap but don't manifest in the repos we've tested (apollo-server uses raw gql template literals, not generated SDK functions)."  # 53a9
- op: discuss  # 9692
  at: '2026-03-18T08:35:16Z'  # 9692
  by: agent  # 9692
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9692
  clock: 12  # 9692
  nonce: '9692'  # 9692
  message: "gRPC codegen investigation (microservices-demo): The existing gRPC linker successfully detects patterns in generated code — 78 routes_to, 6 implements_rpc, 5 grpc_calls edges across Go and Python services. Generated *_pb2_grpc.py (Python) and *_grpc.pb.go (Go) files contain the Register/Stub/Unimplemented patterns the linker matches.\n\nSummary of all codegen areas:\n1. Tauri specta: FIXED (PR #2165)\n2. Electron contextBridge: FIXED (PR #2296)\n3. GraphQL gqlgen (Go): WORKS via implements edges (154 edges in git-bug)\n4. gRPC codegen (Go+Python): WORKS (78+6+5 edges in microservices-demo)\n5. wasm_bindgen facades: Low priority, deferred (WI-pitam)\n\nThe invariant is largely satisfied for the codegen patterns available in our test repos. Moving to holding."  # 9692
